index b98d0625..239c0b5f 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+## [0.37.0] - 2026-11-07
+
 ### Added
 - Polars 2.0 and 2.1 support. The polars requirement is now `>=1.40.0,<2.2`, retaining polars 1.x support while excluding untested minor releases. CI tests polars 2.1 on every Python version and the newest polars 1.x on Python 3.12.
 - `pb.scan_csv`, `pb.scan_parquet`, `pb.read_csv` and `pb.read_parquet`: wrap the Polars readers and record the coordinate system (`zero_based=` required), rename interval columns to `chrom`/`start`/`end`, derive `end` for point data (`end=None`) and optionally convert (`use_zero_based=`) (#486).
@@ -16,12 +18,16 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 - Frame metadata is now owned by polars-bio, replacing the `polars-config-meta` dependency with per-instance storage and a fixed set of propagation methods on ordinary Polars frames. Normal transformation and grouped aggregation chains retain coordinate/source metadata. `config_meta.get_metadata()` returns a shallow snapshot; update entries with `set()`. Generic joins, stacks, and updates clear result metadata, even when input tags agree. The compatibility API is limited to DataFrame/LazyFrame `set()`, `get_metadata()`, and `write_parquet()`; importing the original plugin in the same process is unsupported. See [frame metadata](docs/features/metadata.md) for the method manifest and migration details.
 - LazyFrame inputs to range operations are exported through the public `collect_batches().__arrow_c_stream__()` instead of the private `_inner` attribute.
 - `uv.lock` now pins polars 2.1.0.
+- Updated all `datafusion-bio-format-*` dependencies to v1.15.0 and all `datafusion-bio-function-*` dependencies to v0.24.0. DataFusion remains on 53.0.0 for upstream compatibility (#498).
+- Intel macOS wheels now build on `macos-15-intel`, replacing the retired macOS 14 runner (#497).
 - Range operations raise `MissingCoordinateSystemError` when one input carries coordinate-system metadata and the other does not (an untagged frame or a CSV/Parquet path), also in the default lenient mode. Previously the untagged input was assumed to use the global setting, which shifted results by one position for 0-based data (#486).
 - VCF/BCF paths passed to range operations resolve to the coordinate system the native reader applies: the `zero_based` of the VCF read options passed for that input, otherwise 0-based (the reader default), independent of the global setting. No missing-metadata warning, and no error in strict mode. When a VCF/BCF path is paired with an input of unknown coordinate system (a CSV/Parquet path) in lenient mode, the unknown input is still assumed to use the global setting with a warning, so under the default 1-based setting the pair now raises `CoordinateSystemMismatchError` instead of returning shifted results. Previously a VCF path paired with itself or a 1-based input under the default 1-based setting was filtered as 1-based while read 0-based, shifting results by one position (#486).
 - `merge` and `complement` no longer accept BED file paths (their results were computed with mismatched coordinates); load the file with `pb.scan_bed` and pass the frame (#486).
 - Missing-metadata errors and warnings name the input, the assumed or conflicting system and the reader that matches the input's format; unsupported inputs (BED paths, and every frame + path combination other than a LazyFrame with a CSV/Parquet path and `output_type="polars.LazyFrame"`) are reported before coordinate checks (#486).
 
 ### Fixed
+- BAM scans now support CSI-only indexes, including region filtering and parallel partitioning (#488). GTF CSI indexed scans are also covered by regression tests (#489).
+- `CoordinateSystemMismatchError` now recommends the supported `use_zero_based` reader argument instead of the nonexistent `one_based` argument (#487).
 - `scan_table`/`read_table` with a `schema` failed on polars 2 with `ColumnNotFoundError`. Polars 2 names headerless CSV columns from `column_0` instead of `column_1`; columns are now renamed by position.
 - Errors raised while scanning (for example a DataFusion execution error) surface as `pl.exceptions.ComputeError` again on polars 2. Polars 1.x wrapped them automatically, but polars 2.x does not.
 - Importing polars-bio and calling `pb.set_loglevel()` no longer configure or change the application's root logger, avoiding duplicated messages and interference with custom handlers such as colorlog. Overlap algorithm announcements now use the library logger. The library still defaults to `WARNING`; applications configure logging output themselves (#291).
@@ -29,6 +35,12 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 - `pb.set_option()` raises `ValueError` for unknown or invalid `datafusion.*` options (outside `datafusion.bio.*`) instead of panicking (#484).
 - Collecting the same file-backed scan more than once at a time, for example a self-join on one `scan_vcf()` LazyFrame, `pl.collect_all()`, or several threads, panicked with `Failed to register <format> table: ... already exists` or failed with `Failed to read table`. Every collect now registers its provider under a private name, for all formats, and so does `select()` of GFF/GTF attribute columns.
 
+### Security
+- Updated locked Rust TLS dependencies and Python dependencies to address security advisories, including `aws-lc-rs`, `rustls`, `rustls-webpki`, Pillow, filelock, pypdf, virtualenv, Brotli, nbconvert, certifi and Tornado (#492, #495, #499).
+
+### Packaging
+- The maintained Bioconda recipe drops `polars-config-meta`, includes its bundled license, and allows `polars>=1.40.0,<2.2`. These changes must also be applied to the upstream Bioconda recipe together with the 0.37.0 source version and checksum; autobump does not update dependencies.
+
